Note : 
------
At the start of each simulation session, ensure that the file 
clcd_pl110/SourceMe is sourced to initialise certain environment variables.

Example SourceMe file:
# Set up variables specific to this peripheral macro block
# --------------------------------------------------------
# Set the path environment variable to the peripheral design root directory
# For example clcd_pl110/
setenv PERIPH /home/nbray/work/tryfan/clcd_pl110

# Set the peripheral name abbreviation, for example Clcd
setenv PERIPHERAL Clcd

# Set the ARM Product number for this peripheral, for example pl110
setenv PRODUCT PL110

# VHDL Cell library
# -----------------
# Set the path environment variable to the technology library VITAL timing views
# For VHDL gate level simulations use LIB_VITAL

# Set the generic library path for the Avant! CB25 VITAL library
setenv CB25_VITAL $PERIPH/../../LIBRARIES/avanti/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/vital

# Set the path to the Avant! CB25 VITAL library, standard cell zero delay view
setenv LIB_VITAL $CB25_VITAL/cb25os163/zero

# VERILOG Cell library
# --------------------
# Set the path environment variable to the technology library Verilog timing views
# For Verilog gate level simulations use LIB_VERILOG

# Set the generic library path for the Avant! CB25 Verilog library
setenv CB25_VERILOG $PERIPH/../../LIBRARIES/avanti/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/verilog

# Set the path to the Avant! CB25 VITAL library, standard cell zero delay view
setenv LIB_VERILOG $CB25_VERILOG/cb25os163/zero

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Steps for running BusTalk VHDL simulations. 

The C sources of the test pattern files reside in the
BusTalk/bustests directory.

There are currently eleven test pattern that need to
be run to fully validate the CLCDC:

Check_Large.c
Check_Flat.c
Check_Vertical.c
Check_Retry.c
Check_STNDualC.c
Check_STNDualM.c
Check_STNSingleC.c
Check_STNSingleM.c
Check_TFT.c
IntrTest.c
FreqTest.c (parameter "Ratio" modifiable within this file)

The following instructions should be applied to each of
the above test patterns.

Functional Tests
----------------
1. VHDL RTL simulations
------------------------
- In the BusTalk/bustests directory,
  for each of the respective pattern files 
  'make <pattern file>' 
  This will create the respective invec/<pattern file>.bif
  e.g. make Check_TFT will create invec/Check_TFT.bif

  Change the link from BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.bif
  to the test vector file in BusTalk/bustests/invec/<pattern file>.bif
  For example,
  cd BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/
  ln -s ../../bustests/invec/Check_TFT.bif infile.bif

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL RTL
  uut = $PERIPH/vhdl/uut/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the clcd_pl110/vhdl/uut directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following file:
  In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_Clcd.vhd)

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim tb_Clcd

2. VHDL NETLIST simulations
---------------------------
- In the BusTalk/bustests directory,
  for each of the respective pattern files 
  'make <pattern file>' 
  This will create the respective invec/<pattern file>.bif
  e.g. make Check_TFT will create invec/Check_TFT.bif

  Change the link from BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.bif
  to the test vector file in BusTalk/bustests/invec/<pattern file>.bif
  For example,
  cd BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/
  ln -s ../../bustests/invec/Check_TFT.bif infile.bif

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL NETLIST
  uut = $PERIPH/vhdl/uutNetlist/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the clcd_pl110/vhdl/uutNetlist directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following file:
    In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_Clcd.vhd)

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim +no_glitch_msg -sdfmax u_CLcd=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Clcd_Vhdl_dtype.sdf21 tb_Clcd
  vsim +no_glitch_msg -sdfmin u_CLcd=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Clcd_Vhdl_dtype.sdf21 tb_Clcd

